<sn><md>### What PDF.js Is

PDF.js is a JavaScript library that parses and renders PDF files in the browser (and Node.js) without plugins. It has three layers:

- **Core layer** (`pdf.worker`): parses the PDF binary format. Runs in a Web Worker so the UI never freezes.
- **Display layer** (`pdf.mjs`): the public API you call (`getDocument`, `getPage`, `render`...). It talks to the worker for you.
- **Viewer layer** (`pdf_viewer`): a ready-made UI (zoom, search, thumbnails, sidebar). Optional; you can build your own with the display layer.

The typical flow is: **load document → get page → create viewport → render to canvas**, then optionally add a text layer (selectable text) and an annotation layer (links, forms).


</md></sn><sn><md>### Installation and Setup

- Option A: **CDN** (quickest)

  ```html
  <canvas id="pdf-canvas"></canvas>
  
  ```
  +++ pdf.js
  ```js
  /**
  * PDF.js library + worker.
  * Parsing runs in a Web Worker so the UI stays responsive.
  */
  import * as pdfjsLib from "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/pdfjs-dist@5.4.149/build/pdf.min.mjs";

  pdfjsLib.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc =
  "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/pdfjs-dist@5.4.149/build/pdf.worker.min.mjs";

  export { pdfjsLib };

  ```
  +++

- Option B: **npm**

  ```bash
  npm install pdfjs-dist
  ```

  ```js
  import * as pdfjsLib from 'pdfjs-dist';
  import workerUrl from 'pdfjs-dist/build/pdf.worker.min.mjs?url'; // Vite syntax
  pdfjsLib.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc = workerUrl;
  ```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Key files in `pdfjs-dist/build`

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `pdf.mjs` / `pdf.min.mjs` | Main display-layer API |
| `pdf.worker.mjs` / `pdf.worker.min.mjs` | Parser running in the worker |
| `web/pdf_viewer.mjs` + `pdf_viewer.css` | Prebuilt viewer components and styles |
| `cmaps/` | Character maps for CJK and special fonts |
| `standard_fonts/` | Fallback fonts for PDFs that do not embed fonts |
</md></sn><sn><md>### Quick Start: Render Page 1

```js
const loadingTask = pdfjsLib.getDocument('sample.pdf');
const pdf = await loadingTask.promise;           // PDFDocumentProxy
const page = await pdf.getPage(1);               // PDFPageProxy (1-based!)

const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale: 1.5 });
const canvas = document.getElementById('pdf-canvas');
const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

canvas.width = viewport.width;
canvas.height = viewport.height;

await page.render({ canvasContext: ctx, viewport }).promise;
```

Three objects matter most: 
- **LoadingTask** (progress and cancel), 
- **PDFDocumentProxy** (whole file), 
- **PDFPageProxy** (one page).

</md></sn><sn><md>### Loading: `getDocument(src)`

`getDocument` starts loading and returns a **PDFDocumentLoadingTask**. `src` is either a string URL or a parameters object.

**Loading from different sources**

```js
// 1. URL
pdfjsLib.getDocument('https://example.com/file.pdf');

// 2. Object with options
pdfjsLib.getDocument({ url: 'file.pdf', withCredentials: true });

// 3. Binary data (Uint8Array / ArrayBuffer), e.g. from a file input
input.addEventListener('change', async (e) =&gt; {
  const file = e.target.files[0];
  const data = new Uint8Array(await file.arrayBuffer());
  const pdf = await pdfjsLib.getDocument({ data }).promise;
});

// 4. Base64 string
const raw = atob(base64String);
const bytes = Uint8Array.from(raw, (c) =&gt; c.charCodeAt(0));
pdfjsLib.getDocument({ data: bytes });
```

Note: PDF.js may transfer the buffer to the worker, which detaches it. Pass `data.slice()` if you need to reuse the original array.

</md></sn><sn><md>### Important parameters

| Parameter | Type | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `url` | string | Remote or relative URL |
| `data` | TypedArray / ArrayBuffer / string | Raw PDF bytes |
| `httpHeaders` | object | Custom request headers, e.g. `{ Authorization: 'Bearer x' }` |
| `withCredentials` | boolean | Send cookies on cross-site requests |
| `password` | string | Password for encrypted PDFs |
| `rangeChunkSize` | number | Bytes per range request (default 65536) |
| `disableRange` | boolean | Disable partial (range) loading |
| `disableStream` | boolean | Disable streaming fetch |
| `disableAutoFetch` | boolean | Load only pages that are needed, not the whole file in the background |
| `cMapUrl` | string | Folder URL of `cmaps/` (needed for many CJK PDFs) |
| `cMapPacked` | boolean | Set `true` when using the packed `.bcmap` files |
| `standardFontDataUrl` | string | Folder URL of `standard_fonts/` |
| `useSystemFonts` | boolean | Use locally installed fonts when fonts are not embedded |
| `isEvalSupported` | boolean | Set `false` under strict CSP (no `eval`) |
| `enableXfa` | boolean | Render XFA forms |
| `verbosity` | number | Log level: `0` errors, `1` warnings, `5` infos |

```js
const task = pdfjsLib.getDocument({
  url: 'big.pdf',
  cMapUrl: 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/pdfjs-dist@4.10.38/cmaps/',
  cMapPacked: true,
  standardFontDataUrl: 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/pdfjs-dist@4.10.38/standard_fonts/',
  disableAutoFetch: true,
  disableStream: true,
});
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### PDFDocumentLoadingTask members

| Member | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `promise` | Resolves to the `PDFDocumentProxy` |
| `onProgress` | Callback `({ loaded, total }) =&gt; {}` |
| `onPassword` | Callback `(updatePassword, reason) =&gt; {}` for encrypted files |
| `destroy()` | Cancels loading and frees the worker resources |

```js
const task = pdfjsLib.getDocument('large.pdf');

task.onProgress = ({ loaded, total }) =&gt; {
  if (total) progressBar.value = (loaded / total) * 100;
};

const pdf = await task.promise;
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Password-protected PDFs

```js
const task = pdfjsLib.getDocument('locked.pdf');

task.onPassword = (updatePassword, reason) =&gt; {
  // reason === pdfjsLib.PasswordResponses.NEED_PASSWORD (1) or INCORRECT_PASSWORD (2)
  const pwd = prompt(reason === 2 ? 'Wrong password, try again:' : 'Enter password:');
  updatePassword(pwd);
};

const pdf = await task.promise;
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### PDFDocumentProxy 

The whole document,Obtained from `await task.promise`.

**Properties**

| Property | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `numPages` | Total page count |
| `fingerprints` | Array of unique hashes, handy as a key for saving per-document state (last page, zoom) |
| `loadingTask` | The task that created it |

```js
console.log(`Pages: ${pdf.numPages}`);
const key = 'lastPage:' + pdf.fingerprints[0];
localStorage.setItem(key, 5);
```
</md></sn><sn><md>#### `getPage(pageNumber)`

Returns a `PDFPageProxy`. Page numbers start at **1**. Throws if out of range.

```js
const page = await pdf.getPage(3);
```

#### `getPageIndex(ref)` and `getDestination(id)`

Used to resolve internal links. A destination is an array like `[ref, { name: 'XYZ' }, left, top, zoom]`; `getPageIndex` turns `ref` into a zero-based page index.

```js
async function goToNamedDest(name) {
  const dest = await pdf.getDestination(name);   // array or null
  if (!dest) return;
  const pageIndex = await pdf.getPageIndex(dest[0]);
  renderPage(pageIndex + 1);
}
```

#### `getDestinations()`

Returns an object of all named destinations: `{ name: destArray }`.

</md></sn><sn><md>### `getOutline()`

Returns the table of contents (bookmarks) as a tree, or `null` if none exists. Each item has `title`, `dest` (name or array), `url`, `items` (children), `bold`, `italic`, `color`.

```js
async function buildToc(pdf, container) {
  const outline = await pdf.getOutline();
  if (!outline) { container.textContent = 'No outline'; return; }

  const makeList = (items) =&gt; {
    const ul = document.createElement('ul');
    for (const item of items) {
      const li = document.createElement('li');
      const a = document.createElement('a');
      a.textContent = item.title;
      a.href = '#';
      a.onclick = async (e) =&gt; {
        e.preventDefault();
        let dest = item.dest;
        if (typeof dest === 'string') dest = await pdf.getDestination(dest);
        if (!dest) return;
        const idx = await pdf.getPageIndex(dest[0]);
        renderPage(idx + 1);
      };
      li.append(a);
      if (item.items.length) li.append(makeList(item.items));
      ul.append(li);
    }
    return ul;
  };
  container.append(makeList(outline));
}
```
</md></sn><sn><md>#### `getMetadata()`

Returns `{ info, metadata, contentDispositionFilename, contentLength }`.

```js
const { info, metadata } = await pdf.getMetadata();
console.log(info.Title, info.Author, info.Producer, info.CreationDate);
console.log(info.PDFFormatVersion, info.IsEncrypted);
console.log(metadata?.get('dc:title'));   // XMP metadata, may be null
```

#### `getPageLabels()`

Returns an array of custom labels (for example `['i', 'ii', '1', '2']`) or `null`.

#### `getPermissions()`

Returns an array of permission flags or `null`. Compare with `pdfjsLib.PermissionFlag`.

```js
const perms = await pdf.getPermissions();
if (perms &amp;&amp; !perms.includes(pdfjsLib.PermissionFlag.PRINT)) {
  printBtn.disabled = true;
}
```

#### `getAttachments()`

Returns embedded files: `{ filename: { filename, content: Uint8Array } }` or `null`.

```js
const files = await pdf.getAttachments();
for (const f of Object.values(files ?? {})) {
  const blob = new Blob([f.content]);
  const a = Object.assign(document.createElement('a'), {
    href: URL.createObjectURL(blob), download: f.filename,
  });
  a.click();
}
```

#### `getData()`

Returns the original PDF bytes as a `Uint8Array`, which is useful for a Download button when the PDF came from a file input.

```js
const bytes = await pdf.getData();
const blob = new Blob([bytes], { type: 'application/pdf' });
```

#### `saveDocument()`

Returns bytes of the PDF **including** changes made through annotation or form editing (via `annotationStorage`). Use it instead of `getData()` when the user filled forms or added annotations.

```js
const bytes = await pdf.saveDocument();
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Other document methods

| Method | Returns |
| --- | --- |
| `getJavaScript()` | Array of document-level JavaScript strings or `null` |
| `getFieldObjects()` | Form field info by name or `null` |
| `hasJSActions()` | `true` if the document or fields have JS actions |
| `getOptionalContentConfig()` | Layers (OCG) configuration for toggling layer visibility |
| `getPageMode()` / `getViewerPreferences()` / `getOpenAction()` | Initial view hints stored in the file |
| `getMarkInfo()` | Tagged-PDF information for accessibility |
| `getDownloadInfo()` | `{ length }`, available once the data is loaded |
| `getStats()` | Internal stream and font statistics |
| `cleanup()` | Frees cached resources (call after rendering many pages) |
| `destroy()` | Terminates the worker for this document; call when closing it |

```js
// Closing a document correctly
await pdf.cleanup();
await pdf.destroy();
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### PDFPageProxy 

A single page

**Properties**

| Property | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `pageNumber` | 1-based page number |
| `rotate` | Intrinsic rotation (0, 90, 180, 270) |
| `view` | `[xMin, yMin, xMax, yMax]` page box in PDF points (1 pt = 1/72 inch) |
| `userUnit` | Scale for the page size unit (normally 1) |
| `ref` | Object reference of the page |
</md></sn><sn><md>### `getViewport({ scale, rotation, offsetX, offsetY, dontFlip })`

Creates a `PageViewport`: the mapping between PDF coordinates and screen pixels. `scale: 1` means 72 DPI, so `1.5` gives about 108 DPI. `rotation` is **added** to the page's own rotation.

![view_port_diagram](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/Programming/Documentation/Javascript%20Library/assets/view_port_diagram.jpeg)


```js
const vp = page.getViewport({ scale: 1 });
const vpRotated = page.getViewport({ scale: 1, rotation: (page.rotate + 90) % 360 });

// Fit to container width
const base = page.getViewport({ scale: 1 });
const fitWidth = page.getViewport({ scale: container.clientWidth / base.width });
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### `render(params)`

Draws the page and returns a **RenderTask**.

| Parameter | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `canvasContext` | 2D context to draw into (v5 also accepts `canvas`) |
| `viewport` | Result of `getViewport()` |
| `transform` | `[a, b, c, d, e, f]` extra matrix, used for HiDPI |
| `background` | CSS color for the page background (default white); `'rgba(0,0,0,0)'` for transparent |
| `intent` | `'display'` (default) or `'print'` |
| `annotationMode` | `pdfjsLib.AnnotationMode.DISABLE`, `ENABLE`, `ENABLE_FORMS`, `ENABLE_STORAGE` |
| `optionalContentConfigPromise` | Custom layer visibility |

RenderTask members: `promise` and `cancel()`.

**Sharp rendering on HiDPI / Retina screens:**

```js
async function renderCrisp(page, canvas, scale) {
  const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
  const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale });

  canvas.width = Math.floor(viewport.width * dpr);
  canvas.height = Math.floor(viewport.height * dpr);
  canvas.style.width = Math.floor(viewport.width) + 'px';
  canvas.style.height = Math.floor(viewport.height) + 'px';

  const transform = dpr !== 1 ? [dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0] : null;
  await page.render({
    canvasContext: canvas.getContext('2d'),
    viewport,
    transform,
  }).promise;
}
```

**Avoiding render collisions (zoom spam):** a canvas can only have one active render. Cancel the previous one first.

```js
let currentTask = null;

async function safeRender(page, canvas, scale) {
  if (currentTask) {
    currentTask.cancel();
    currentTask = null;
  }
  const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale });
  canvas.width = viewport.width;
  canvas.height = viewport.height;
  currentTask = page.render({ canvasContext: canvas.getContext('2d'), viewport });
  try {
    await currentTask.promise;
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.name !== 'RenderingCancelledException') throw err;
  } finally {
    currentTask = null;
  }
}
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### `getTextContent(params)`

Returns `{ items, styles }`. Each item in `items` is a text run with `str`, `transform` (matrix: `[scaleX, skewY, skewX, scaleY, x, y]`), `width`, `height`, `dir`, `fontName`, `hasEOL`. Useful params: `includeMarkedContent`, `disableNormalization`.

```js
// Extract all text from a document
async function extractAllText(pdf) {
  let out = '';
  for (let i = 1; i &lt;= pdf.numPages; i++) {
    const page = await pdf.getPage(i);
    const content = await page.getTextContent();
    out += content.items.map((it) =&gt; it.str + (it.hasEOL ? '\n' : '')).join('') + '\n\n';
    page.cleanup();
  }
  return out;
}
```

**Simple search across pages:**

```js
async function searchPdf(pdf, term) {
  const hits = [];
  const needle = term.toLowerCase();
  for (let i = 1; i &lt;= pdf.numPages; i++) {
    const page = await pdf.getPage(i);
    const { items } = await page.getTextContent();
    const text = items.map((it) =&gt; it.str).join(' ').toLowerCase();
    let idx = text.indexOf(needle);
    while (idx !== -1) {
      hits.push({ page: i, snippet: text.slice(Math.max(0, idx - 30), idx + 50) });
      idx = text.indexOf(needle, idx + needle.length);
    }
  }
  return hits;
}
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### `streamTextContent(params)`

Same data as `getTextContent` but as a `ReadableStream`. This is what `TextLayer` consumes internally; use it for very large pages.

### `getAnnotations({ intent })`

Returns an array of annotation objects: links, form widgets, highlights, notes. Common fields: `subtype`, `rect`, `url`, `dest`, `contents`, `fieldType`, `fieldName`, `fieldValue`, `color`.

```js
const annots = await page.getAnnotations();
const links = annots.filter((a) =&gt; a.subtype === 'Link' &amp;&amp; a.url);
console.log(links.map((l) =&gt; l.url));

const fields = annots.filter((a) =&gt; a.subtype === 'Widget');
fields.forEach((f) =&gt; console.log(f.fieldType, f.fieldName, f.fieldValue));
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### `getOperatorList()`

Returns low-level drawing operations (`{ fnArray, argsArray }`). Compare `fnArray` values with `pdfjsLib.OPS`. Useful to detect and extract images.

```js
const ops = await page.getOperatorList();
const imageOps = ops.fnArray.filter((fn) =&gt; fn === pdfjsLib.OPS.paintImageXObject).length;
console.log(`Images on page: ${imageOps}`);
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Other page methods

| Method | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `getStructTree()` | Tagged-PDF structure (headings, paragraphs) for accessibility |
| `getXfa()` | XFA form tree if the page is XFA |
| `cleanup(resetStats?)` | Releases page resources; call after you finish with a page |
</md></sn><sn><md>## PageViewport (coordinates and scaling)

| Member | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `width`, `height` | Size in CSS pixels at the chosen scale |
| `scale`, `rotation` | The values used to create it |
| `viewBox` | The page's box in PDF space |
| `transform` | The 6-number matrix mapping PDF to viewport |
| `convertToViewportPoint(x, y)` | PDF point → `[x, y]` on screen |
| `convertToPdfPoint(x, y)` | Screen point → PDF point |
| `convertToViewportRectangle([x1, y1, x2, y2])` | PDF rectangle → screen rectangle |
| `clone({ scale, rotation, ... })` | New viewport with overrides |

**Example: click on the canvas and get PDF coordinates**

```js
canvas.addEventListener('click', (e) =&gt; {
  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
  const x = e.clientX - r.left;
  const y = e.clientY - r.top;
  const [pdfX, pdfY] = viewport.convertToPdfPoint(x, y);
  console.log('PDF coordinates:', pdfX, pdfY);
});
```

**Example: draw a box over a link annotation**

```js
for (const a of annots.filter((a) =&gt; a.subtype === 'Link')) {
  const [x1, y1, x2, y2] = viewport.convertToViewportRectangle(a.rect);
  const box = document.createElement('div');
  Object.assign(box.style, {
    position: 'absolute',
    left: Math.min(x1, x2) + 'px',
    top: Math.min(y1, y2) + 'px',
    width: Math.abs(x2 - x1) + 'px',
    height: Math.abs(y2 - y1) + 'px',
    outline: '1px solid red',
  });
  pageWrapper.append(box);
}
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Text Layer 

selectable, searchable text

The canvas is only an image. To let users select and copy text, overlay a transparent layer of positioned `<span>` elements. Use the `TextLayer` class (exported from the main module in v4+) together with `pdf_viewer.css` (or at least the `.textLayer` rules).

```html
<div id="page" style="position:relative">
  <canvas id="canvas"></canvas>
  <div id="text-layer" class="textLayer"></div>
</div>
```

```js
async function renderWithText(page, scale) {
  const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale });
  const canvas = document.getElementById('canvas');
  canvas.width = viewport.width;
  canvas.height = viewport.height;
  await page.render({ canvasContext: canvas.getContext('2d'), viewport }).promise;

  const textDiv = document.getElementById('text-layer');
  textDiv.replaceChildren();
  textDiv.style.setProperty('--scale-factor', viewport.scale);   // required by the CSS
  textDiv.style.width = viewport.width + 'px';
  textDiv.style.height = viewport.height + 'px';

  const textLayer = new pdfjsLib.TextLayer({
    textContentSource: page.streamTextContent(),
    container: textDiv,
    viewport,
  });
  await textLayer.render();
}
```

`TextLayer` members: `render()` (returns a promise), `cancel()`, `textDivs` (array of created spans), `textContentItemsStr` (their strings; handy for highlighting search hits), `update({ viewport })` for re-layout on zoom.
</span></md></sn><sn><md>### Annotation Layer (links, forms)

The `AnnotationLayer` creates clickable links and form widgets over the canvas. Links need a **link service** that knows how to navigate; the prebuilt `SimpleLinkService` (from `pdf_viewer`) or `PDFLinkService` are typical choices.

```js
const annotations = await page.getAnnotations({ intent: 'display' });

const annotationLayer = new pdfjsLib.AnnotationLayer({
  div: annotationDiv,
  accessibilityManager: null,
  annotationCanvasMap: null,
  page,
  viewport: viewport.clone({ dontFlip: true }),
});

await annotationLayer.render({
  annotations,
  div: annotationDiv,
  page,
  viewport: viewport.clone({ dontFlip: true }),
  linkService,                      // object with goToDestination, getDestinationHash, etc.
  renderForms: true,
});
```

If you only need working external links and do not want the full layer, the manual approach from section 7 (place `<a>` elements at converted rectangles) is a simple, dependable alternative.
