```js
console.log(pdfjsLib.version);                      // '4.10.38'
console.log(pdfjsLib.Util.normalizeRect([100, 50, 10, 5]));  // [10, 5, 100, 50]
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### The Prebuilt Viewer Components

When you want a complete viewer without writing everything yourself, use `pdf_viewer.mjs`:

| Class | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `EventBus` | Publish/subscribe bus all components share (`pagesinit`, `pagechanging`, `scalechanging`, `updatefindmatchescount`...) |
| `PDFLinkService` | Handles internal/external links and navigation |
| `PDFFindController` | Search with highlighting, whole word, case sensitivity |
| `PDFViewer` | Manages page rendering, virtual scrolling, zoom, rotation |
| `PDFHistory` | Browser history integration |
| `PDFThumbnailViewer` | Sidebar thumbnails |

```js
import * as pdfjsLib from 'pdfjs-dist';
import { EventBus, PDFViewer, PDFLinkService, PDFFindController } from 'pdfjs-dist/web/pdf_viewer.mjs';
import 'pdfjs-dist/web/pdf_viewer.css';

const container = document.getElementById('viewerContainer'); // must be position:absolute with overflow:auto
const eventBus = new EventBus();
const linkService = new PDFLinkService({ eventBus });
const findController = new PDFFindController({ eventBus, linkService });

const viewer = new PDFViewer({
  container,
  eventBus,
  linkService,
  findController,
});
linkService.setViewer(viewer);

eventBus.on('pagesinit', () =&gt; {
  viewer.currentScaleValue = 'page-width';   // 'auto' | 'page-fit' | 'page-actual' | number
});

const pdf = await pdfjsLib.getDocument('sample.pdf').promise;
viewer.setDocument(pdf);
linkService.setDocument(pdf, null);

// Controls
viewer.currentPageNumber = 4;       // go to page
viewer.currentScale = 1.25;         // zoom
viewer.pagesRotation = 90;          // rotate
viewer.increaseScale();
viewer.decreaseScale();

// Search
eventBus.dispatch('find', {
  query: 'invoice', caseSensitive: false, highlightAll: true,
  phraseSearch: true, findPrevious: false,
});
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Complete Mini Viewer

```html



  <input type="file" id="file" accept="application/pdf">
  <button id="prev">Prev</button>
  <button id="next">Next</button>
  <span id="info"></span>
  <button id="zoomOut">-</button>
  <button id="zoomIn">+</button>
  <div><canvas id="canvas"></canvas></div>

  


```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Error Handling

The loading promise rejects with named exceptions:

| `error.name` | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `InvalidPDFException` | File is corrupt or not a PDF |
| `MissingPDFException` | URL not found (404) |
| `UnexpectedResponseException` | Server returned an unexpected HTTP status |
| `PasswordException` | Password needed or wrong (`error.code` 1 or 2) |
| `AbortException` | Loading was cancelled with `destroy()` |
| `RenderingCancelledException` | A render was cancelled with `cancel()` (normal, not a real error) |

```js
try {
  const pdf = await pdfjsLib.getDocument(url).promise;
} catch (err) {
  switch (err.name) {
    case 'MissingPDFException': alert('File not found.'); break;
    case 'InvalidPDFException': alert('This is not a valid PDF.'); break;
    case 'PasswordException': alert('Password required.'); break;
    default: console.error(err);
  }
}
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Performance Best Practices

1. **Render only visible pages.** Use `IntersectionObserver` and render a page when it approaches the viewport; the prebuilt `PDFViewer` already does this.
2. **Call `page.cleanup()`** after finishing with a page and `pdf.cleanup()` after bulk work, to free memory.
3. **Cancel stale renders** when the user zooms or flips pages quickly.
4. **Limit canvas size.** Browsers cap canvas area (roughly 16 to 268 megapixels depending on device). Clamp `scale * dpr` for huge pages.
5. **Keep the worker.** Create the worker once; do not recreate it per document. Call `destroy()` on documents you are done with.
6. **Use range requests.** Server must send `Accept-Ranges: bytes` and CORS headers exposing `Content-Range`, `Content-Length`, `Accept-Ranges`; then large files open instantly.
7. **Render thumbnails small.** Use a low scale (0.2 to 0.3) and `intent: 'display'`.

</md></sn><sn><md>### Troubleshooting

| Problem | Cause and fix |
| --- | --- |
| *Setting up fake worker failed* | `workerSrc` is missing or points to a wrong file/version. Match worker and library versions exactly. |
| CORS error on a remote PDF | The server must allow your origin (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin`). Otherwise fetch it through your own backend. |
| Blurry canvas | Account for `devicePixelRatio` (section 6). |
| Missing or garbled CJK/special characters | Set `cMapUrl` and `cMapPacked: true`. |
| Wrong fonts when fonts are not embedded | Set `standardFontDataUrl` or `useSystemFonts: true`. |
| *Cannot use the same canvas during multiple render() operations* | Cancel the previous `RenderTask` first. |
| `getPage` throws *Invalid page request* | Page numbers are 1-based and must be within `1..numPages`. |
| Text layer misaligned | `--scale-factor` CSS variable not set, or `pdf_viewer.css` is not loaded. |
| Works locally but not from `file://` | Browsers block modules and workers on `file://`. Serve with a local server (`npx serve`). |
| `Buffer is detached` | Data array was transferred to the worker. Pass a copy (`data.slice()`). |

</md></sn><sn><md>### Cheat Sheet

```js
// Load
const pdf = await pdfjsLib.getDocument(src).promise;

// Info
pdf.numPages;  await pdf.getMetadata();  await pdf.getOutline();

// Page
const page = await pdf.getPage(n);
const vp = page.getViewport({ scale: 1.5, rotation: 0 });

// Draw
await page.render({ canvasContext: ctx, viewport: vp }).promise;

// Text and links
const text = await page.getTextContent();
const annots = await page.getAnnotations();

// Save and close
const bytes = await pdf.saveDocument();
page.cleanup();  await pdf.destroy();
```
